    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "If the points $(3,a)$, $(-12,b)$ and $(c,-12)$ lie on the line with equation $y=-\\frac23x$, find the values of $a$, $b$ and $c$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=-2,\\quad b=8,\\quad c=18$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}a&=-\\frac23\\times3=-2\\\\b&=-\\frac23\\times(-12)=8\\\\-12&=-\\frac23c\\\\-36&=-2c\\\\c&=18\\end{aligned}$$",
